        "position": { "x": 40, "y": 20 },
        "data": {
          "instanceTitle": "How this graph works",
          "text": "# DDPM-style denoising on a synthetic **p(x)** in ℝ²\n\n**What is being learned:** The trainer feeds **x₀** rows from the dataset’s **input** tensor into the diffusion objective (noise prediction MSE). Targets **y** are unused for this task.\n\n**Synthetic ground truth:** `dataset_mixer` concatenates batches from two `linear_dataset` children with the same **inputDim=2** but different **inputDistribution** (uniform on [−1,1]² vs standard normal). With **proportionA** between 0 and 1, **x₀** follows a **two-component mixture**—a simple closed-form toy where the score network must capture two modes.\n\n**Model:** `diffusion_score_model` is ε_θ(x_t, t) (see `comfy_research/engine/diffusion_score_model.py`). Pair it only with `diffusion_mse_loss`.\n\n**Try:** Adjust **proportionA**, **trainTotalSamples**, **diffusionTimesteps T**, or switch one branch to `random_noise_dataset` for a pure-noise mode."
        }
      },
